                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b176ea3f-3c56-3ffa-a629-b7c4ab9a84aa",
                        "entry_id": "905fc2e3-56f1-3729-ba76-9bb8ca79515f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To interpret or adapt based on the moral and aesthetic philosophy of Friedrich Schiller."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebfa9dda-f8fe-4cda-9ac3-40fb1452e08c",
                                "sense_id": "b176ea3f-3c56-3ffa-a629-b7c4ab9a84aa",
                                "text": "Thus Costa gave a lead to all those adapters who have laboured to over-Schillerize the opera, and to eliminate Charles V from it. '"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95b7e51d-8f27-4c7f-863b-02cd8d901653",
                                "sense_id": "b176ea3f-3c56-3ffa-a629-b7c4ab9a84aa",
                                "text": "In 1859 he advises Lassalle to 'Shakespearize' rather than to “Schillerize'. Shakespeare he regards as the supreme poet of the modern world; Schiller seems to him aesthetically unsound and counter-revolutionary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "beb6805f-5fd8-4e0d-b6e0-68f8523e2d04",
                                "sense_id": "b176ea3f-3c56-3ffa-a629-b7c4ab9a84aa",
                                "text": "My intention is not to use Schiller as some kind of fall-guy – there is not a text written today which is not Schillerized."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
